{"id": "sdqa0111", "pool": "sdqa", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The United States officially pulled out of Vietnam in 1 9 73. That year, the Paris Peace Accords were signed, which officially ended direct U. S. involvement in the Vietnam War. However, the last American troops actually left the country later that year, around November 1 97 2 or early 197 3, depending on the unit. So while the agreement was signed in January 1 973, the withdrawal process continued for several months afterward.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 27, "carrier_ended": null}
